# ─── Required in production ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Grades written quiz answers against the reviewer's reference answer. Without
# it the final test loads and then fails to mark anything.
#
# Set a monthly spend cap on this key in the Anthropic console. There are no
# accounts, so the grading route cannot tell one visitor from another and the
# in-process rate limiter resets every time Lambda recycles. The cap is the only
# real bound on the bill.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Signs quiz attempt tokens, which carry the sampled question ids between
# serving and grading — it is what stops a learner asking to be graded against
# a question they were not given. Any random string of 32+ characters:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Rotating it invalidates every in-flight attempt.
QUIZ_ATTEMPT_SECRET=

# ─── Optional: product analytics ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave blank to collect nothing.
#
# Nobody is identified — there are no accounts — so these describe anonymous
# browsers, not people. Requests are proxied through /ingest so an ad blocker
# cannot remove them. Session replay and autocapture are off, because this app
# has people's finances on screen.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ─── Local only. Never set in production. ────────────────────────────────────
# Used by `npm run ingest` to pull candidate videos. The deployed app makes no
# TikHub calls at all, so this key never leaves your machine.
# Scope needed: /api/v1/tiktok/app/v3/
TIKHUB_API_KEY=
